---
args: { input: CaseInput }
returns: RunProposal
---
1. Bind `goal = await frameRequest(input)` from the request and `policy = await selectPolicy(input)` from supplied authority candidates. Preserve unresolved precedence instead of guessing which source governs.
2. Bind `work = await formTaskGraph(goal)` and `evidencePlan = await planEvidence(input, work)` so each operation has explicit prerequisites and a searched source universe.
3. Run the stages in their dependency order. The first stage receives only `input.domainRecords.firstStage`; every later stage receives the preceding function's actual accepted records. Bind each full result separately.
const interpretPreferencesResult = await interpretPreferences(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan);
const modelPlotsResult = await modelPlots(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, interpretPreferencesResult.accepted);
const generatePlansResult = await generatePlans(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, modelPlotsResult.accepted);
const negotiateAllocationResult = await negotiateAllocation(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, generatePlansResult.accepted);
const coordinateSeasonResult = await coordinateSeason(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, negotiateAllocationResult.accepted);
4. Bind `stageSet: CaseStageSet = { interpretPreferences: interpretPreferencesResult, modelPlots: modelPlotsResult, generatePlans: generatePlansResult, negotiateAllocation: negotiateAllocationResult, coordinateSeason: coordinateSeasonResult }` and `collection: CollectionFinding = await reconcileCollection(stageSet)`. Bind `allQuestions: string[] = [...interpretPreferencesResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...modelPlotsResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...generatePlansResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...negotiateAllocationResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...coordinateSeasonResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...collection.coverageGaps]` and `questions: QuestionBatch = await resolveQuestions(allQuestions, input)`.
5. Bind `invalidation = await assessDelta(input)`, `review = await prepareReview(collection)`, and `view = await composeView(review, input)`; pass each child its actual declared inputs and retain the returned object.
6. Bind `allChecks: CheckResult[] = [...interpretPreferencesResult.checks, ...modelPlotsResult.checks, ...generatePlansResult.checks, ...negotiateAllocationResult.checks, ...coordinateSeasonResult.checks]`. Bind `hasGateFailure = allChecks.some(check => check.verdict !== "pass")` and `hasBlocker = input.authorityStatus !== "authorized" || questions.questions.length > 0 || collection.coverageGaps.length > 0`. Bind `disposition: "proposed" | "blocked" | "needs-review" = hasBlocker ? "blocked" : hasGateFailure ? "needs-review" : "proposed"`. Bind `rationale: string[] = allChecks.map(check => `${check.check}: ${check.verdict}; evidence ${check.evidenceIds.join(",")}`)`.
7. Operational detail 1 — A member becomes unavailable: renegotiate duties instead of silently assigning them to someone else. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (renegotiate duties instead of silently assigning them to someone else.) through the existing stage result for GardenPreference; preserve exact source/version and the prior GardenPreference, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
8. Operational detail 2 — A shared tool breaks: replan affected tasks and preserve reservations awaiting repair. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (replan affected tasks and preserve reservations awaiting repair.) through the existing stage result for GardenPreference; preserve exact source/version and the prior GardenPreference, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
9. Operational detail 3 — A plot’s condition is uncertain: request appropriate assessment before consequential changes. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (request appropriate assessment before consequential changes.) through the existing stage result for GardenPreference; preserve exact source/version and the prior GardenPreference, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
10. Operational detail 4 — A trial allocation succeeds: seek explicit agreement before making it permanent. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (seek explicit agreement before making it permanent.) through the existing stage result for GardenPreference; preserve exact source/version and the prior GardenPreference, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
11. Operational detail 5 — A member leaves mid-season: transfer care and harvest rights through a documented agreement. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (transfer care and harvest rights through a documented agreement.) through the existing stage result for GardenPreference; preserve exact source/version and the prior GardenPreference, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
12. Initialize `revisions: RevisionProposal[] = []`. If any gate is not pass, bind `revision = await proposeRevision(the failed check names, the smallest affected stage name)` and add that returned proposal to revisions. Bind and return `result: RunProposal = { caseId: input.caseId, goal, policy, work, evidencePlan, interpretPreferences: interpretPreferencesResult, modelPlots: modelPlotsResult, generatePlans: generatePlansResult, negotiateAllocation: negotiateAllocationResult, coordinateSeason: coordinateSeasonResult, collection, questions, invalidation, review, view, revisions, disposition, rationale }`. Proposed actions remain proposals. The host owns authorization, persistence, effect dispatch and verification.
